# Build artefacts.
# next-env.d.ts and tsconfig.tsbuildinfo are regenerated by `next build` and `tsc`; committing them
# produces a diff on every build that reviews nothing.
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# `generated/` predates ADR-007 — it was where `prisma generate` would have written its client, and
# nothing writes there now. The entry stays because `eslint.config.mjs` and `tsconfig.json` still
# exclude the same path, and three files agreeing about a directory that does not exist costs
# nothing while two of three agreeing would read as an oversight.
generated/

# Supabase CLI local state. `supabase/.temp/` holds the CLI's own scratch files and `.branches/` its
# branch metadata; neither is source and both are per-machine. `supabase/migrations/` and
# `supabase/types.generated.ts` ARE source and are committed — the migrations are the schema, and the
# generated types are what keeps `pnpm typecheck` offline (ADR-007 OQ-2).
#
# The CLI also writes its own `supabase/.gitignore` covering the same two paths. They are named here
# as well because this is the file a reader opens to learn what the repository does not track.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
